Duties and responsibilities at this level will entail: -
Implementing existing Supply Chain Management policies, strategies, regulations, guidelines, manuals and procedures;
Implementation of e-procurement strategies;
Drafting communication of outcomes of procurement evaluations and service delivery;
Conducting market research, surveys and analysis;
Drafting procurement and disposal, programmes, plans, strategies and budgets;
Sourcing of suppliers;
Carrying out stock taking, stock control and stock audit;
Preparing agenda and minutes of tender/procurement committee;
Preparing of tender and contract documents;
Providing support to end users on procurement guidelines;
Safeguarding tenders, quotations and request for proposals;
Initiating disposal of unserviceable stores;
Certifying invoices and payment vouchers to suppliers;
Implementing procurement plans and processing requisitions;
Reviewing preparation of technical specifications; and
Drafting tender advertisement notices
Qualifications and Experience
For appointment to this grade, one must have:-
Satisfactorily served for a cumulative period of six years, three of which should have been at Supply Chain Management Officer I, Grade NCPD 7 or its equivalent position in a comparable organization
Bachelor’s degree in any of the following disciplines: Supply Chain, Business Administration or Commerce (Supply Chain Management option), Procurement or equivalent qualification from a recognized institution;
Membership of Kenya Institute of Supplies Management (KISM) or Chartered Institute of Purchasing and Supplies (CIPS);
Proficiency in computer application;
Demonstrated merit and ability as reflected in work performance and results;
